        "content": "## Summary\n\n**Target fact**: `F:ml430-nat-coprime-add-self-right-c3ed0f45` \n**Statement**: `∀ {m n : ℕ}, m.Coprime (n + m) ↔ m.Coprime n`\n\n**Structural shape**: This is a biconditional (iff) about coprimality preservation under addition. It states that `m` is coprime to `n + m` if and only if `m` is coprime to `n`. The pattern involves adding one argument to itself within a coprimality predicate.\n\n**Dependencies**: The fact has no dependencies and would unlock one downstream fact (`F:ml430-nat-coprime-self-add-right-966e5434`).\n\n**Available premises**: The nat prelude contains only 2 coprime-related theorems (`Nat.coprime_of_bezout_one`, `Nat.coprime_of_lt_prime`) but has 7 gcd theorems including `Nat.gcd_bezout`, `Nat.gcd_dvd_left/right`, and `Nat.gcd_succ`. Since coprimality is typically defined as `gcd = 1`, these gcd theorems are the working premises.\n\n**Similar eligible facts**: The frontier contains a closely related sibling `F:ml430-nat-coprime-add-self-left-5e93448c` with statement `∀ {m n : ℕ}, (m + n).Coprime n ↔ m.Coprime n` (left-side addition variant). There are also other coprime facts involving dvd relationships.\n\n**Registry status**: No operations currently target this fact.",
